# Deployment Summary

The Spring Boot banking demo is ready for Azure App Service deployment from the existing workspace assets. The application builds successfully into a WAR package, and the repository already contains the Azure App Service deployment workflow, infrastructure template, and Azure Developer CLI metadata needed for deployment.

## What was validated
- Maven packaging produced [target/banking-demo-0.0.1-SNAPSHOT.war](../target/banking-demo-0.0.1-SNAPSHOT.war).
- The app is configured to expose health endpoints and use the Azure-provided port via [src/main/resources/application.properties](../src/main/resources/application.properties).
- The deployment files in [infra/appservice.bicep](../infra/appservice.bicep) and [.github/workflows/azure-app-service.yml](../.github/workflows/azure-app-service.yml) are aligned with a Java 21 WAR deployment target.

## Remaining manual actions
1. Create or select the Azure resource group and App Service resources.
2. Configure the required GitHub Actions secrets.
3. Trigger the deployment workflow or deploy the generated WAR manually.
4. Validate the deployed site at `https://<app-name>.azurewebsites.net/health`.
